Z||000004||Haze||06-27-2001||01:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sjp777:<BR><B>I'm ready to go with black carpet. Since ACC is down and Mr Mikes no longer sells them it seems my only alternative is fiero store.<P>From what I understand it is supposed to install over the stock carpet. That would be great for more sound deadening, but how does it fit? I'm worried it might interfere with the full clutch pedal travel.<P>Anybody have the scoop on it?<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not sure what your talking about... "install over the stock carpet" But I just bought a carpet kit with extra door carpet (from The Fiero Store) & it was made by ACC. It replaces the old carpet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cooltext2087.jpg">  </A>||||reg||10
Z||000005||Monkeyman||06-27-2001||05:03 AM||||Mr. Mike suggests pulling the backing off of the new carpet and laying it down on top of the old carpet.  He's given this advice to countless buyers over the years and I haven't heard anything bad about it so far.  Just make sure you remove the backing/insulation from the new carpet.  If in doubt, just call Mr. Mike himself.  He'll explain it to ya.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||06-27-2001||09:02 AM||||First; That the ACC web site is down does not mean that the company is out of business. C'mon guys! A web site is not a company. Is just another option. Use the phone!<BR>Second; The carpet that Mr. Mike sold to me didn't have any back pad. So he did recommend me to install it over my original. I did that and it came out very nice (see my URL). If ACC's comes with padding then I think you will have to remove the original. Otherwise it will be too thick in some places like the clutch pedal and others.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DecadenceR||06-27-2001||05:53 PM||||Haze - That door carpet, was it ready to install or did you have to fo gluing and stuff like that? I'm debating on what way to go when I'm ready.||||reg||1
